[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/463349136","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/6386#issuecomment-463349136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/6386","id":463349136,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MzM0OTEzNg==","user":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-13T20:09:27Z","updated_at":"2019-02-13T20:09:27Z","body":"Mypy has special treatment of `assert isinstance(obj, ...)`, they work as runtime-checked casts, and are normally used to narrow types. In your case it actually widens the type. I would say, we should not widen type after an assert (unless I am missing some use cases).\r\n\r\nAnyway, IIUC you should just do this:\r\n```python\r\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\r\n\r\n...\r\n\r\nif not TYPE_CHECKING:\r\n    assert isinstance(newtype, type(M))\r\n\r\n...\r\n```\r\n(Another question is that we use runtime expression -- function call -- for static checks, which is probably bad.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/463349136/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/463364694","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/6386#issuecomment-463364694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/6386","id":463364694,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MzM2NDY5NA==","user":{"login":"rldleblanc","id":11397591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzk3NTkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11397591?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc","html_url":"https://github.com/rldleblanc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-13T20:51:14Z","updated_at":"2019-02-13T20:51:14Z","body":"> Mypy has special treatment of `assert isinstance(obj, ...)`, they work as runtime-checked casts, and are normally used to narrow types. In your case it actually widens the type. I would say, we should not widen type after an assert (unless I am missing some use cases).\r\n\r\nI don't know that I'm widening the type. My class `T` (is actually an implementation of an ABC) that requires MixIn `M` to work properly. The ABC has base functionally and requires `A` at a minimum. Class `MA` has both `M` and `A` which satisfies the specific needs of class `T` and has the generic stuff to satisfy the ABC of class `T`. So, I just want to make sure that `M` is only accepted for class `T` which returns objects of class `A` which could be an `MA` object. What you proposed looks like an acceptable solution. Too bad types aren't enforced at run time, it would make all this simpler.\r\n\r\n> Anyway, IIUC you should just do this:\r\n> \r\n> ```python\r\n> from typing import TYPE_CHECKING\r\n> \r\n> ...\r\n> \r\n> if not TYPE_CHECKING:\r\n>     assert isinstance(newtype, type(M))\r\n> \r\n> ...\r\n> ```\r\n\r\n> (Another question is that we use runtime expression -- function call -- for static checks, which is probably bad.)\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what you mean by this. Are you talking about the `newtype:Type[MYTYPES]=MA` in `def __init__(self, newtype:Type[MYTYPES]=MA) -> None:`? I'm still pretty new at all of this.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/463364694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rldleblanc","id":11397591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzk3NTkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11397591?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc","html_url":"https://github.com/rldleblanc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rldleblanc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2143938142,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIxNDM5MzgxNDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/2143938142","actor":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i